# invokegeo

- Label: Invoke Geometry
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2048
- Parameters: 4 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/invokegeo.html
- Summary (EN): Runs a program saved in geometry on the layers wired into the node. The program is typically created by wiring a Block to Geometry COP into the program input.
- Résumé (FR) : Exécute sur les couches d'entrée un programme COP sauvegardé en géométrie, avec itérations, à partir d'un bloc Block to Geometry.

- Inputs meaning: ["program_geometry: compiled program geometry from Block to Geometry", "input#: source layers; their count and details come from the Inputs settings"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Iterations", "meaning": "how many times the program runs, each run's outputs feeding the next run's inputs"}, {"name": "Set Inputs and Outputs from Incoming Program", "meaning": "populates the Inputs and Outputs multiparameters from the program signature"}, {"name": "Input Label / Input Type", "meaning": "name and data type of each input; the label must match an Input Name on the Block Begin COP"}, {"name": "Output Label / Output Type", "meaning": "name and data type of each output; the label must match an Output Name on the Block End COP"}]

- Caveats: ["Repeated iterations work only when outputs convert to matching inputs by index; otherwise a single iteration runs with a warning."]

